; $VER: AROSTCP-netautoconf 1.3 (2.10.2026)
; AROSTCP-netautoconf (c) The AROS Dev Team.
;
; Build a usable configuration in ENV: when the machine has none.
;
; Nothing populates ENVARC:AROSTCP on a fresh install, and a Live CD has no
; writable ENVARC: at all, so ${AROSTCP/AutoRun} is empty and the stack never
; starts - the system comes up with a browser and no network. ENV: is RAM on
; every AROS system, so a configuration written here works on read-only media
; too; it simply does not survive a reboot, which is what Prefs/Network and
; ENVARC: are for.
;
; Only called when ENV:AROSTCP/Config does not exist, so a machine configured
; through Prefs/Network keeps its own settings.
;
If NOT EXISTS ENV:AROSTCP
  MakeDir >NIL: ENV:AROSTCP
EndIf
If NOT EXISTS ENV:AROSTCP/db
  MakeDir >NIL: ENV:AROSTCP/db
EndIf

; The shipped db carries hosts/protocols/services and friends but no
; interfaces file - that is the one we write here.
Copy >NIL: SYS:System/Network/AROSTCP/db ENV:AROSTCP/db ALL QUIET NOREQ

; Ask netdetect which adapter is present.
;
; A USB adapter wins: one that is plugged in is the one the user means. Only
; USB network devices Poseidon has already loaded are tried, and only a unit
; that opens is used, so nothing is loaded from disk.
;
; Otherwise netdetect identifies the PCI card by enumerating PCI and matching
; vendor/product IDs against the drivers AROS ships - it never opens a PCI
; driver. That matters: e1000's Close() does not stop the unit (its own
; FIXME), so an open/close probe consumes the driver's one-time bring-up and
; the stack that opens afterwards inherits an unconfigured unit and moves no
; traffic. Reading PCI costs nothing and leaves AROSTCP as the card's first
; opener.
;
; One interface is written: dhclient supports a single interface only.
;
netdetect INTERFACES ENV:AROSTCP/db/interfaces IFNAME eth0 QUIET

If NOT WARN
  ; SetEnv, not Echo: Echo appends a newline, and Package-Startup's
  ; ${AROSTCP/AutoRun} eq "True" then compares against "True\n" and never
  ; matches - the config looks right on disk and the stack still never starts.
  SetEnv AROSTCP/Config "ENV:AROSTCP/db"
  SetEnv AROSTCP/AutoRun "True"
EndIf
